From: Harshit Gupta <39994376+arelyx@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 18:41:41 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 64/65] freedreno/xenos: native quads, quad strips and polygons

Xenos draws them itself (Xenia kQuadList 0x0d, kQuadStrip 0x0e, kPolygon
0x0f). In line polygon mode only their outer edges are drawn, which the
triangles Mesa split them into couldn't do (piglit polygon-mode; a quad in
line mode lit 237 pixels, the diagonal included, now 191). Long quad
lists/strips split in multiples of 4; long polygons go through the
triangle-list conversion like fans.

